by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-02T05:52:06Z

I applied the rework discussed above, keeping @Seb33300 as the author of the commit:

- `PRE_VALIDATE` is gone; `POST_VALIDATE` is the one event this PR adds.
- The event now lives on `FormEvents` and in the `Symfony\Component\Form\Event` namespace, next to the other form events, so the extra `ValidatorFormEvents` class is not needed anymore. It is also registered in `FormEvents::ALIASES`.
- The dispatch is now a stateless walk of the form tree in `ValidationListener::validateForm()`, children first, root last. This removes the shared `$dispatchEvents` state and its accumulation issue, and leaves `FormTypeValidatorExtension` unchanged.
- The walk skips buttons (`ButtonBuilder::getEventDispatcher()` throws) and unsubmitted children (`$clearMissing = false`), and keeps the `hasListeners()` guard.
- `PostValidateEvent::setData()` throws, like `PostSubmitEvent::setData()` does.
- The tests are rewritten as functional ones on a real form factory, covering dispatch order, whole-tree validity seen from a child, errors added by a child listener being seen by parent listeners, and the skipped cases. The previous test relied on `setMethods()`, which no longer exists in current PHPUnit.

The doc PR symfony/symfony-docs#17229 will need the matching update.
